# Docker workspace COPY

Root `package.json` uses `"workspaces": ["packages/*"]`. `npm install` in the image only sees folders you copy. **Do not COPY unused sibling packages** to “satisfy” the lockfile.

Copy `core` plus packages this image’s `package.json` / e2e suite imports.

```dockerfile
# dialect e2e (postgres/mysql/sqlite pattern)
COPY packages/core/package.json packages/core/tsconfig.json ./packages/core/
COPY packages/sqlite/package.json packages/sqlite/tsconfig.json ./packages/sqlite/

# ORM e2e: adapter + the suite dialect (E2E_SUITE is postgres or mysql)
COPY packages/sequelize/package.json packages/sequelize/tsconfig.json ./packages/sequelize/
COPY packages/${E2E_SUITE}/package.json packages/${E2E_SUITE}/tsconfig.json ./packages/${E2E_SUITE}/

# example: only deps from examples/<app>/package.json
COPY packages/core ./packages/core
COPY packages/sqlite ./packages/sqlite
```

`FROM docker.io/library/node:26-alpine`. Build context is the repo root.
